# Git on Windows runs with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites CRLF to LF on
# commit for anything it guesses is text. It guessed wrong about the explainer
# video and the two PNGs: committing them stripped every 0x0D that happened to
# precede an 0x0A inside the compressed data, silently corrupting all three
# (the mp4 lost 135 bytes and would no longer play). Nothing caught it, because
# the diff of a binary file reads only "Bin 7656856 -> 7656721 bytes".
#
# Order matters: the last matching line wins for a given attribute, so the
# catch-all goes first and the binary rules override it. Add new binary
# extensions below, in the same breath as the first such file.
* text=auto

*.mp4 binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
